= Phuong Luu Vo
Associate Professor, Department of Communications Engineering, Example University

~~~
{}{img_left}{images/portrait.svg}{Portrait of Phuong Luu Vo}{175}{}{}
Welcome! I am an Associate Professor in the Department of Communications Engineering at
Example University, where I lead the *Wireless Networks and Optimization (WNO) Group*.

My research sits at the boundary between communication theory and optimization: I work on
resource allocation, stochastic and convex optimization, learning-based network control, and
the performance analysis of emerging wireless systems such as reconfigurable intelligent
surfaces and large antenna arrays. Please have a look at my [publications.html Publications]
and at the work of my [students.html research group].

I am currently looking for motivated students for *prethesis*, *thesis*, and *internship*
projects. Before you write to me, please read the [prospective.html Prospective Students]
page carefully -- it explains the whole process, the requirements, and the topics that are
currently open.
~~~

