== Research at a glance

A large part of our work can be written as a resource allocation problem. For a single-cell
network with $K$ users sharing a total power budget $P_{\max}$, where $p_k$ denotes the power
allocated to user $k$ and $h_k$ its channel gain, a typical design problem is

\(
\begin{array}{ll}
\mbox{maximize} & \displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{K} \log_2\!\left(1 + \frac{p_k\,h_k}{\sigma^2}\right) \\
\mbox{subject to} & \displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{K} p_k \le P_{\max}, \qquad p_k \ge 0, \quad k = 1,\ldots,K .
\end{array}
\)

We are interested both in the structure of the optimal solution and in algorithms that find it
with limited channel state information. See the [publications.html Publications] page for the
papers that came out of this line of work, and [mathjax-test.html this page] if you want to
check that the mathematics on this site renders correctly in your browser.

